====Article====
{{pt-article}}

# {{senseid|pt|article}} [[the]] {{n-g|(the definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable...)}}
## {{n-g|(...because it has already been mentioned, is to be completely specified in the same sentence, or very shortly thereafter)}}
##: {{ux|pt|Estou lendo '''o''' livro que Maria avaliou.|t=I’m reading '''the''' book Mary reviewed.}}
## {{n-g|(...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge)}}
### {{n-g|(used before a noun designating something considered to be unique, or of which there is only one at a time)}}
###: {{ux|pt|Deus salve '''a''' Rainha!|t=God save '''the''' Queen!}}
### {{n-g|(used to indicate a certain example of (a noun) which is usually of most concern or most common or familiar)}} 
###: {{ux|pt|Me leva pr'''o''' aeroporto.|t=Take me to '''the''' airport.}}
### {{n-g|(used as an alternative to a [[possessive pronoun]]), sometimes after {{m|pt|lhe}}, especially when referring to a body part, a family member, or a pet.}}
###: {{ux|pt|'''O''' pai está viajando.|t='''My''' dad is traveling.|lit='''The''' dad is traveling.}}
###: {{ux|pt|Infelizmente, um ladrão roubou-lhe '''o''' celular.|t=Unfortunately, a robber stole '''her''' phone.|lit=Unfortunately, a robber stole [from] her '''the''' phone.}}
### {{lb|pt|colloquial}} {{n-g|(precedes a familiar nickname or other term of address)}}
###: {{ux|pt|Como tá '''a''' Bia hoje?|t=How's '''the''' Beats today?|footer="How are you today, Beats?"}}
### {{n-g|(used in many idiomatic expressions and proverbs to refer to common objects, roles, or situations connected with something definite, in the manner of an analogy)}}
###: {{m|pt|pior a emenda que o soneto|pior '''a''' emenda que '''o''' soneto}}
### {{n-g|(when stressed, indicates that it describes something which is considered to be best or exclusively worthy of attention)}}
###: {{ux|pt|Esse é <u>'''o'''</u> hospital ideal para se realizar uma cirurgia cardíaca.|t=That is <u>'''the'''</u> hospital to go to for heart surgery.}}
### {{n-g|(when stressed, used before the name of a famous person, to distinguish said person from a hypothetical lesser-known person with the same name)}}
###: {{ux|pt|Me chamo Ivete, mas não sou <u>'''a'''</u> [[w:Ivete Sangalo|Ivete]].|t=My name is Ivete, but I'm not <u>'''the'''</u> Ivete.}}
### {{n-g|(used before a noun phrase beginning with superlative or comparative adjective or an ordinal number, indicating that the noun refers to a single item)}}
###: {{ux|pt|Que '''o''' melhor homem vença.|t=May '''the''' better man win.}}
### {{n-g|(introducing a singular term to be taken generically: preceding a name of something standing for a whole class)}}
###: {{ux|pt|'''O''' carvalho é uma árvore grande.|t='''The''' oak is a big tree.}}
### {{n-g|(used with the singular or plural of a surname to indicate the entire family)}}
###: {{ux|pt|'''Os''' Bush(es) ocupam cargos políticos há várias décadas, e '''os''' Kennedy(s) há ainda mais tempo.|t='''The''' Bushes have held political office for several decades and '''the''' Kennedys longer.}}
# {{n-g|Makes any phrase into a {{glossary|substantive}}.}}
#* '''2009''', [[w:Holy Bible|Bíblia Sagrada]], edition [[w:João Ferreira de Almeida|Almeida Revista e Corrigida]], [[w:pt:Sociedade Bíblica do Brasil|Brazilian Bible Society]], [[w:Book of 1 Samuel|1 Samuel]] 15:22
#: {{uxa|pt|Porém Samuel disse: Tem, porventura, o Senhor tanto prazer em holocaustos e sacrifícios, como em que se obedeça à palavra do Senhor? Eis que '''o''' obedecer é melhor do que '''o''' sacrificar; e '''o''' atender melhor é do que a gordura de carneiros.|t=But Samuel said, "Does the Lord take as much pleasure in burnt offerings and sacrifices as in obeying the Lord? Behold, obeying is better than sacrificing, and heeding is better than the fat of rams."}}

=====Usage notes=====
For the most part, usage of the definite article in Portuguese is the same as in English. Some differences include:
* it is optionally but commonly used with abstract mass nouns:
*: {{ux|inline=1|pt|'''O''' amor é melhor que '''a''' guerra.|Love is better than war.}}
* in Brazil, it can be optionally used with adjectival possessive pronouns, and mandatorily with substantival possessive pronouns; both are mandatory in Portugal:
*: {{ux|inline=1|pt|('''O''') meu livro é melhor que '''o''' seu.|My book is better than yours.}}
* it can be used with personal names; often this indicates familiarity with the person (due to personal connection with them or because they are famous); this is avoided in formal contexts:
*: {{ux|inline=1|pt|('''O''') João foi até a cidade.|João went to the city.}}
*: {{ux|inline=1|pt|('''O''') Einstein foi um cientista famoso.|Einstein was a famous scientist.}}
* it is much more commonly used with placenames than it is in English; most names of countries, states, provinces and continents take the definite article, as well as a few cities:
*: {{ux|inline=1|pt|Eu moro n'''o''' Luxemburgo.|I live in Luxembourg.}}
*: {{ux|inline=1|pt|'''O''' Rio de Janeiro fica n'''o''' Brasil.|Rio de Janeiro is in Brazil.}}

